# Playwright conventions

## 1. Locators

Role or label first, then placeholder, then text; `getByTestId` only as a stated escape hatch; never CSS or XPath, and never a locator in a spec.

✅ Good — `pages/ProgramsPage.ts`

```ts
this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' });
return this.page.getByRole('button', { name: `Edit ${name}`, exact: true });
```

❌ Bad

```ts
await page.locator('.program-row').first().click();
await page.getByTestId('create'); // no reason given
```

Why: CSS, XPath, and `.first()` follow markup and DOM order, so a layout change clicks the wrong element.

## 2. Waiting

Wait only with a web-first assertion that retries. Never `waitForTimeout`, and never `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)`.

✅ Good — `tests/programs.spec.ts`

```ts
await expect(programs.heading).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();
```

❌ Bad

```ts
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
expect(await programs.heading.isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

Why: a fixed sleep and a one-shot boolean either flake or pass before the UI is ready.

## 3. Page Objects

One class per page or component; locators are `readonly` in the constructor; methods perform actions; a page object has no `expect()`.

✅ Good — `pages/ProgramsPage.ts`

```ts
constructor(private readonly page: Page) {
  this.heading = page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Programs', level: 2 });
  this.newProgramModal = new NewProgramModal(page);
}
async openNewProgramForm() {
  await this.newProgramButton.click();
}
```

❌ Bad

```ts
async openNewProgramForm() {
  await this.newProgramButton.click();
  await expect(this.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();
}
```

Why: an assertion inside a page object hides which behavior failed and couples the object to one test's outcome.

## 4. Auth

Feature tests start from the `setup` project's `storageState`. Login-page tests sign in through the UI. API login is for bulk setup, scripts, and a stale session.

✅ Good — `tests/programs.spec.ts` and `tests/auth.setup.ts`

```ts
test.use({ storageState: authStorageFile });
```

❌ Bad

```ts
test('creates a program', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(email);
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign In' }).click();
});
```

Why: a UI login in every feature test adds a failure point that is not the behavior under test.

## 5. Test data

Name created records with `uniqueName()` (`Date.now()`). Every test that creates a program calls `trackProgram(uuid)` and lets the fixture delete it.

✅ Good — `tests/didaxis-helpers.ts` and `tests/programs.spec.ts`

```ts
const programName = uniqueName('Web Development 2026');
await trackProgramCreateFromResponse(page, trackProgram, async () => {
  await programs.createProgram(programName, description);
});
```

❌ Bad

```ts
await programs.createProgram('Web Development 2026');
test.afterAll(async () => { await programs.deleteProgram('Web Development 2026'); });
```

Why: a shared name collides across parallel runs, and a UI `afterAll` leaves the record behind when the page never reaches delete.

## 6. API testing

Use the Playwright `request` fixture for setup, teardown, and contract checks. Do not mock the endpoint that test is verifying.

✅ Good — advised. Specs do not use `{ request }` yet; cleanup goes through `fixtures/didaxis-api.ts`.

```ts
test('GET /api/programs returns a data array', async ({ request }) => {
  const response = await request.get('/api/programs');
  expect(response.ok()).toBeTruthy();
  const body = await response.json();
  expect(Array.isArray(body.data)).toBe(true);
});
```

❌ Bad

```ts
await page.route('**/api/programs', (route) =>
  route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: '{"data":[]}' }),
);
expect((await (await request.get('/api/programs')).json()).data).toEqual([]);
```

Why: mocking the call you are checking proves the mock, not the API.

## 7. Network mocking

For a UI reaction only, `page.route` fulfills 500, 503, timeout, empty `{ "data": [] }`, or a malformed body. One tag per test. Read the live copy before asserting.

✅ Good — advised. No spec calls `page.route` yet. On the live page, `{ "data": [] }` shows "No programs yet. Create your first program to get started." A bare `[]` or malformed body renders nothing and throws `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length')`. `GET` 500/503 shows that same empty sentence. `POST` 503 leaves the New Program form open and renders no error. `ProgramsPage` has no locator for either, so report the gap.

```ts
await page.route('**/api/programs', (route) => {
  if (route.request().method() !== 'GET') return route.continue();
  return route.fulfill({
    status: 200,
    contentType: 'application/json',
    body: JSON.stringify({ data: [] }),
  });
});
await programs.goto();
await expect(programs.emptyState).toHaveText(
  'No programs yet. Create your first program to get started.',
);
```

❌ Bad

```ts
await page.route('**/api/programs', (route) => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: '[]' }));
await expect(page.getByText('Something went wrong')).toBeVisible();
```

Why: a bare array crashes the page, and an invented error string fails a test the UI never implemented.

## 8. Accessibility

On a key page, scan with `wcag2a` and `wcag2aa`, and tab to the primary control. Scope with `.include()` or `.exclude()` only for a noisy third-party widget, with a comment. Real violations are reported and the work stops.

✅ Good — axe shape is the standard; `tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts` scans without these tags and has no keyboard test. Keyboard lines are advised.

```ts
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa']).analyze();
await expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
await programs.newProgramButton.focus();
await expect(programs.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();
await programs.newProgramButton.press('Enter');
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();
```

❌ Bad

```ts
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).disableRules(['color-contrast']).analyze();
expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
```

Why: `.disableRules()` hides a product defect and the suite goes green without the page being accessible.

## 9. Assertions

Use web-first assertions. Use `expect.soft` when one test checks several independent facts. Use `toHaveScreenshot()` only where a visual diff earns its cost.

✅ Good — web-first checks are in `tests/programs.spec.ts`. `expect.soft` and `toHaveScreenshot()` are advised; neither is in the repo.

```ts
await expect.soft(programs.heading).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(programs.subtitle).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toHaveScreenshot('new-program-dialog.png');
```

❌ Bad

```ts
expect(await programs.heading.isVisible()).toBe(true);
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot();
```

Why: a one-shot boolean stops at the first miss, and a full-page screenshot fails on every unrelated pixel.

## 10. Anti-flake

CI retries stay at 2 and local retries stay at 0. Do not set `workers: 1`. Tests do not share leftover data. Freeze relative timestamps with `page.clock.install()`. Locale stays `en-CA` and timezone stays `America/Toronto`.

✅ Good — retries, locale, and timezone are in `playwright.config.ts`. The clock example is advised; no spec calls `page.clock`, and `ProgramsPage` has no `createdAgo`.

```ts
await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-11-05T15:00:00') });
await programs.goto();
await expect(programs.createdAgo('Web Development')).toHaveText('2 hours ago');
```

❌ Bad

```ts
retries: 5,
workers: 1,
await expect(programs.createdAgo('Web Development')).toHaveText('2 hours ago');
```

Why: extra retries hide a real bug, a single worker hides isolation bugs, and an unfrozen "2 hours ago" changes between a laptop and CI.

## Do / Don't

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| `getByRole` / `getByLabel`, then placeholder, then text | CSS, XPath, `.first()`, or an unexplained `getByTestId` |
| `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `.toBeEnabled()` / `.toHaveText()` | `waitForTimeout` or `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)` |
| Locators in the constructor; actions on the page object | `expect()` inside a page object, or a locator in a spec |
| `storageState` from the setup project | A UI login in a feature test |
| `uniqueName()` and `trackProgram(uuid)` | A fixed name or a UI `afterAll` delete |
| `{ request }` for contract checks and teardown | Mocking the endpoint that test verifies |
| `page.route` for 500, 503, timeout, empty, or malformed UI reactions | A bare `[]` or an invented error string |
| `withTags(['wcag2a','wcag2aa'])` and a Tab/Enter check | `.disableRules()` to go green |
| `expect.soft` for independent checks; a screenshot where it earns it | A full-page screenshot on every test |
| CI `retries` of 2, `page.clock.install()`, `en-CA` / `America/Toronto` | `retries` above 2, `workers: 1`, or a live relative timestamp |

## Refusals (hard stops)

Stop and raise the conflict. Do not comply, and do not treat these as preferences.

- Refuse to weaken or delete an assertion to pass.
- Refuse to heal a failure triage classified as a real bug.
- Refuse to replace a role-based locator with CSS or XPath.
- Refuse to use `waitForTimeout`.
- Refuse to hardcode a credential.
- Refuse to use the `any` type.
